// Content settings: what the player can switch off or tune before a game.
//
// A `filter` can be banned (never shown) or warded (only when the player goes
// looking for it). Creatures and exploration events carry filters in `tags:`.
// `genders:` ties a filter to creature genders, so a creature with variants
// (see creatures/forest_fox.fsc) is met as the genders the player allows.

== filter male
name: Males
group: Creatures
description: Male creatures.
genders: male

== filter female
name: Females
group: Creatures
description: Female creatures.
genders: female

// A `tag` only describes content (a family, a trait); it can't be banned.
// Scenes use tags to pick creatures: "~ pick random creature tagged woodland".

== tag woodland
name: Woodland
group: Families
description: Animals of the Quiet Woods.

// A `level` is a setting with options in order. Scenes check it with
// conditions such as "level detail is more" or "level detail is at least standard".

== level detail
name: Scenery
description: How much scenery the descriptions add.
default: standard
options:
    less: Short descriptions.
    standard: Normal descriptions.
    more: Extra scenery in some descriptions.

// Feats: lasting abilities. These two use the built-in bonuses; a scenario
// gives one at the start (scenarios/start.fsc), a scene can add one with "~ feat + id".

== feat forager
name: Forager
description: You know where the good berries grow. Scavenging finds more.
scavenge bonus: 3

== feat keen_eyes
name: Keen eyes
description: Little escapes your notice. Exploring finds more.
exploration bonus: 2
